 PROMPT = """A customer of an online shop searched for: {query}
 
-Pick up to {limit} products from the list that best match the search, best first.
-Answer with one product per line, as: ID | one short reason, addressed to the customer
+Pick up to {limit} products from the list that genuinely suit the search, best first.
+Only include a product if it is the kind of thing the customer is looking for.
+Do not pad the answer: popularity, rating or price alone are not reasons to include
+a product, and fewer than {limit} picks is fine. If nothing in the list suits the
+search (the item is not sold, the word is unknown or misspelt beyond recognition,
+or the brand is not carried), answer with exactly: NONE
+Otherwise answer with one product per line, as: ID | one short reason that says why it
+suits this search, addressed to the customer
 
 Products (ID | name | price | rating out of 5):
 {products}
